{"id":"claim:phon/glides-w-y--coda-glides-form-diphthongs","revision":1,"topic":"topic:phon/glides-w-y","topics":["topic:phon/glides-w-y","topic:phon/glides-w-y--diphthong-analysis"],"statement":{"en":"In syllable-final position, semivowels /w/ and /y/ are realized as [u] and [i], forming diphthongs with the preceding vowel.","ja":"音節末尾において、半母音 /w/ と /y/ は [u] および [i] として実現され、先行する母音とともに二重母音を形成する。"},"type":"alternation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":["syllable-final position"]},"forms":["w","y"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0062-18","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0063-13","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-06-38-590Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:phon/glides-w-y--when-the-prefixes-i-indefinite-object-or-u","revision":1,"topic":"topic:phon/glides-w-y","topics":["topic:phon/glides-w-y","topic:phon/glides-w-y--accent-glide"],"statement":{"en":"When the prefixes i- (indefinite object) or u- (reciprocal) occur intervocalically in an accent-bearing position, they turn into a glide and form a syllable with the following vowel.","ja":"接頭辞 i-（不定目的語）または u-（相互）がアクセント担持位置で母音間に現れる場合、半母音化して後続母音と一つの音節を形成する。"},"type":"alternation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":["intervocalic","in accent-bearing position"]},"forms":["i-","u-"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2022@handbook-epub/l0134-17","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-06-38-590Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:phon/glides-w-y--initial-y-is-deleted-following-a-coda-n","revision":1,"topic":"topic:phon/glides-w-y","topics":["topic:phon/glides-w-y","topic:phon/glides-w-y--boundary-yi-wi-wu"],"statement":{"en":"Initial y- is deleted following a coda -n.","ja":"語末子音 -n に後続する語頭の y- は消去される。"},"type":"alternation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["-n-"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:murasaki2025@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0096-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-06-38-590Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:phon/glides-w-y--initial-y-drops-after-m-or-s-and","revision":1,"topic":"topic:phon/glides-w-y","topics":["topic:phon/glides-w-y","topic:phon/glides-w-y--boundary-yi-wi-wu"],"statement":{"en":"Initial y- drops after -m or -s, and initial w- assimilates to a preceding -m.","ja":"-m や -s の後で語頭の y- が消失し、また -m の後で語頭の w- が同化する。"},"type":"alternation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["-m-","-s-","-mm-"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:murasaki2025@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0096-05","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-06-38-590Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:phon/glides-w-y--initial-y-alternates-to-n-after-coda-h","revision":1,"topic":"topic:phon/glides-w-y","topics":["topic:phon/glides-w-y","topic:phon/glides-w-y--boundary-yi-wi-wu"],"statement":{"en":"Initial y- alternates to -n- after coda -h.","ja":"語末の -h の後で語頭の y- は -n- に交替する。"},"type":"alternation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["-hn-"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:murasaki2025@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0096-06","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-06-38-590Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:phon/glides-w-y--when-another-element-precedes-a-word-beginning-with","revision":1,"topic":"topic:phon/glides-w-y","topics":["topic:phon/glides-w-y","topic:phon/glides-w-y--boundary-yi-wi-wu"],"statement":{"en":"When another element precedes a word beginning with vowels i or u, vowel weakening can occur, shifting i → y and u → w.","ja":"母音 i, u で始まる語の前に別の要素が来ると、母音弱化により i → y、u → w のように子音の y, w に変化する現象がある。"},"type":"alternation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"possible","conditions":["preceded by another element, typically a prefix"]},"forms":["i","u","y","w"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0038-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-06-38-590Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:phon/glides-w-y--vowel-weakening-i-y-u-w-is-frequently","revision":1,"topic":"topic:phon/glides-w-y","topics":["topic:phon/glides-w-y","topic:phon/glides-w-y--boundary-yi-wi-wu"],"statement":{"en":"Vowel weakening (i → y, u → w) is frequently observed in the Saru and Chitose dialects.","ja":"母音弱化（i → y、u → w）は沙流・千歳方言でよく見られる。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/saru","doculect:hokkaido/chitose"],"quantifier":"usually","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0038-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-06-38-590Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:phon/glides-w-y--semivowelization-occurs-in-clusters-such-as-n-s","revision":1,"topic":"topic:phon/glides-w-y","topics":["topic:phon/glides-w-y","topic:phon/glides-w-y--consonant-analysis"],"statement":{"en":"Semivowelization occurs in clusters such as -n + s- becoming -ys-, -V + 'i- becoming -Vy-, -V + 'u- becoming -Vw-, -V + 'a becoming -Vya-, and 'u + 'V- becoming -wVV-.","ja":"-n + s- が -ys- に、-V + 'i- が -Vy- に、-V + 'u- が -Vw- に、-V + 'a が -Vya- に、'u + 'V- が -wVV- に半母音化する。"},"type":"alternation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["-ys-","-Vy-","-Vw-","-Vya-","-wVV-"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:murasaki2025@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0096-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-06-38-590Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:phon/glides-w-y--phonetically-y-is-almost-identical-to-i-but","revision":1,"topic":"topic:phon/glides-w-y","topics":["topic:phon/glides-w-y","topic:phon/glides-w-y--consonant-analysis"],"statement":{"en":"Phonetically /-y/ is almost identical to [i], but phonologically it behaves as a consonant that forms a single syllable with the preceding vowel, cannot bear accent, and is pronounced more weakly than /i/.","ja":"/-y/ は発音上はほとんど /i/ と同じだが、音韻論的には子音扱いであり、前の母音と一緒にひとつの音節を形成し、アクセントが載ることもなく、/i/ より弱く発音される。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["-y","aynu","kamuy"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0029-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-06-38-590Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:phon/glides-w-y--phonetically-w-is-almost-identical-to-u-but","revision":1,"topic":"topic:phon/glides-w-y","topics":["topic:phon/glides-w-y","topic:phon/glides-w-y--consonant-analysis"],"statement":{"en":"Phonetically /-w/ is almost identical to [u], but phonologically it behaves as a consonant that forms a single syllable with the preceding vowel, cannot bear accent, and is pronounced more weakly than /u/.","ja":"/-w/ は発音上はほとんど /u/ と同じだが、音韻論的には子音扱いであり、前の母音と一緒にひとつの音節になり、アクセントが載ることもなく、/u/ より弱く発音される。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["-w","ohaw","kewtum"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0029-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-06-38-590Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:phon/glides-w-y--a-transitional-glide-watari-between-vowels-is-not","revision":1,"topic":"topic:phon/glides-w-y","topics":["topic:phon/glides-w-y","topic:phon/glides-w-y--consonant-analysis"],"statement":{"en":"A transitional glide (watari) between vowels is not a phoneme, so non-phonemic [y] and [w] appearing between vowels are not written in phonemic transcription.","ja":"音素間の移行部で生じる「わたり」は音素ではないため、母音間に現れるわたりとみなされる [y] や [w] は音素表記されない。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["y","w"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0032-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-06-38-590Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:phon/glides-w-y--the-transitional-y-in-iyomante-from-prefix-i","revision":1,"topic":"topic:phon/glides-w-y","topics":["topic:phon/glides-w-y","topic:phon/glides-w-y--consonant-analysis"],"statement":{"en":"The transitional [y] in [iyomante] (from prefix /i-/ and verb /omante/) and [w] in [uwenewsar] (from prefixes /u-/, /e-/ and verb /newsar/) are non-phonemic glides and are transcribed phonemically as /iomante/ and /uenewsar/.","ja":"[iyomante]（接頭辞 /i-/＋動詞 /omante/）の [y] や [uwenewsar]（接頭辞 /u-/、/e-/＋動詞 /newsar/）の [w] はわたり音であり、音韻的にはそれぞれ /iomante/、/uenewsar/ と表記される。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"example_only","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["iomante","uenewsar","omante","newsar","i-","u-","e-"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0032-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-06-38-590Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:phon/glides-w-y--the-word-for-eloquence-has-the-stem-paw","revision":1,"topic":"topic:phon/glides-w-y","topics":["topic:phon/glides-w-y","topic:phon/glides-w-y--consonant-analysis"],"statement":{"en":"The word for 'eloquence' has the stem /paw/ rather than pa with an epenthetic glide, meaning there are two roots for 'mouth': /pa/ and /paw/.","ja":"「雄弁」の語幹はわたりではなく音素 /w/ を含む /paw/ であり、「口」の語根としては /pa/ と /paw/ の二つが存在する。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["pa","paw","pawetok","pawasnu"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0033-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-06-38-590Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:phon/glides-w-y--the-w-in-iwor-hunting-ground-is-the","revision":1,"topic":"topic:phon/glides-w-y","topics":["topic:phon/glides-w-y","topic:phon/glides-w-y--consonant-analysis"],"statement":{"en":"The [w] in /iwor/ 'hunting ground' is the realization of the phoneme /w/, not a transitional glide.","ja":"「猟場」を表す /iwor/ の [w] はわたりではなく、音素 /w/ の実現した形である。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["iwor"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0033-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-06-38-590Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:phon/glides-w-y--the-phonemic-form-of-the-verb-for-to","revision":1,"topic":"topic:phon/glides-w-y","topics":["topic:phon/glides-w-y","topic:phon/glides-w-y--consonant-analysis"],"statement":{"en":"The phonemic form of the verb for 'to hurt' is /iunin/, and the phonetic [y] in [iyunin] is a transitional glide rather than a phoneme.","ja":"「痛む」という動詞の音韻形は /iunin/ であり、[iyunin] の [y] は音素ではなくわたり音である。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/chitose","doculect:hokkaido/southwest/saru"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["iunin"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0038-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-06-38-590Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:phon/glides-w-y--in-the-y-w-consonant-alternation-yakumo-characteristically","revision":1,"topic":"topic:phon/glides-w-y","topics":["topic:phon/glides-w-y","topic:phon/glides-w-y--consonant-analysis"],"statement":{"en":"In the y:w consonant alternation, Yakumo characteristically takes w where other dialects take y, and Horobetsu and Obihiro take y where other dialects take w.","ja":"子音交替 y:w において、他方言が y を持つところで八雲が w を持ち、他方言が w を持つところで幌別と帯広が y を持つことが特徴的である。"},"type":"alternation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/yakumo","doculect:hokkaido/southwest/horobetsu","doculect:hokkaido/central/tokachi"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["puyár","puwár","suyóp","suwóp"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawafukazawa2022@handbook-epub/l0050-13","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-06-38-590Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:phon/glides-w-y--in-hokkaido-ainu-the-semivowels-y-w-serve","revision":1,"topic":"topic:phon/glides-w-y","topics":["topic:phon/glides-w-y","topic:phon/glides-w-y--diphthong-analysis"],"statement":{"en":"In Hokkaido Ainu, the semivowels /y, w/ serve as the second vowel of a diphthong in syllable-coda position.","ja":"北海道アイヌ語において、半母音/y, w/は音節末では重母音の第二母音となる。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":["音節末"]},"forms":["y","w","toy","pewre","ya","wen"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:itabashi2001@pdftotext-pieces/l0002-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-06-38-590Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:phon/glides-w-y--in-sakhalin-ainu-the-semivowels-y-and-w","revision":1,"topic":"topic:phon/glides-w-y","topics":["topic:phon/glides-w-y","topic:phon/glides-w-y--diphthong-analysis"],"statement":{"en":"In Sakhalin Ainu, the semivowels /y/ and /w/ function as the second vowel of a diphthong in syllable-final position.","ja":"樺太アイヌ語において、半母音/y, w/は音節末では重母音の第二母音となる。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":["in syllable-final position"]},"forms":["y","w"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:itabashi2001@pdftotext-pieces/l0003-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-06-38-590Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:phon/glides-w-y--in-kuril-ainu-y-and-w-in-syllable","revision":1,"topic":"topic:phon/glides-w-y","topics":["topic:phon/glides-w-y","topic:phon/glides-w-y--diphthong-analysis"],"statement":{"en":"In Kuril Ainu, /y/ and /w/ in syllable-final position become the second vowel of a diphthong.","ja":"千島アイヌ語において、/y, w/は音節末では重母音の第二母音となる。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:kuril"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":["in syllable-final position"]},"forms":["y","w"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:itabashi2001@pdftotext-pieces/l0005-08","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-06-38-590Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:phon/glides-w-y--diphthongs-include-ai-ui-oi-au-iu-eu","revision":1,"topic":"topic:phon/glides-w-y","topics":["topic:phon/glides-w-y","topic:phon/glides-w-y--diphthong-analysis"],"statement":{"en":"Diphthongs include ai, ui, oi, au, iu, eu, ou, ei, and ae, all of which are falling diphthongs.","ja":"二重母音には ai, ui, oi, au, iu, eu, ou, ei, ae 等があり、すべて下降式である。"},"type":"existence","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["ai","ui","oi","au","iu","eu","ou","ei","ae"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0015-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-06-38-590Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:phon/glides-w-y--among-diphthongs-ou-ei-and-ae-are-extremely","revision":1,"topic":"topic:phon/glides-w-y","topics":["topic:phon/glides-w-y","topic:phon/glides-w-y--diphthong-analysis"],"statement":{"en":"Among diphthongs, ou, ei, and ae are extremely rare: ou occurs only in kokou 'son-in-law', ei is formed when short e is emphasized, and ae occurs only word-initially through rapid contraction of a- and e-.","ja":"重母音のうち ou, ei, ae の用例は極めて少なく、ou は kokou（婿）のみ、ei は短母音 e の強調時に成立し、ae は語頭で第一人称接頭辞 a- と指相接辞 e- の結合が急言された場合にのみ成立する。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["ou","ei","ae","kokou","a-","e-"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0015-05","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-06-38-590Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:phon/glides-w-y--when-an-unstressed-u-or-i-follows-a","revision":1,"topic":"topic:phon/glides-w-y","topics":["topic:phon/glides-w-y","topic:phon/glides-w-y--diphthong-analysis"],"statement":{"en":"When an unstressed /u/ or /i/ follows a vowel, it may be realized as non-syllabic [w] and [y], respectively.","ja":"無強勢の/u/または/i/が母音の後に続く場合、それぞれ非音節的な[w]および[y]に置き換えられることがある。"},"type":"alternation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"possible","conditions":["when an unstressed /u/ or /i/ follows a vowel"]},"forms":["u","i","w","y"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0066-05","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-06-38-590Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:phon/glides-w-y--the-glides-y-and-w-can-occur-in","revision":1,"topic":"topic:phon/glides-w-y","topics":["topic:phon/glides-w-y","topic:phon/glides-w-y--diphthong-analysis"],"statement":{"en":"The glides y and w can occur in syllable-coda position as well as onset position.","ja":"y, w は「矢」，「輪」の頭音と同じだが，これらの音は音節の末尾にも立つ"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["y","w"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0027-08","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-06-38-590Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:phon/glides-w-y--words-such-as-nay-and-haw-are-monosyllabic","revision":1,"topic":"topic:phon/glides-w-y","topics":["topic:phon/glides-w-y","topic:phon/glides-w-y--diphthong-analysis"],"statement":{"en":"Words such as nay and haw are monosyllabic, where y and w are pronounced lightly and briefly following the vowel.","ja":"nay, haw はこれ以上区切って発音することが普通はできない一音節の単語であり，y や w は母音に添えて軽く短く発音される。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["nay","haw","y","w"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0028-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-06-38-590Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:phon/glides-w-y--diphthongs-such-as-ai-ui-and-au-involve","revision":1,"topic":"topic:phon/glides-w-y","topics":["topic:phon/glides-w-y","topic:phon/glides-w-y--diphthong-analysis"],"statement":{"en":"Diphthongs such as ai, ui, and au involve devocalization of the second vowel, leading to pronunciations [aj], [uj], and [aw].","ja":"ai, ui, au などの二重母音は後半の母音の非音節化を伴い、[aj], [uj], [aw] のように発音される。"},"type":"alternation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["ai","ui","au","ay","uy","aw"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:shibatani1990@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0014-05","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-06-38-590Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:phon/glides-w-y--the-semivowels-w-and-y-do-not-occur","revision":1,"topic":"topic:phon/glides-w-y","topics":["topic:phon/glides-w-y","topic:phon/glides-w-y--marginal-syllables"],"statement":{"en":"The semivowels /w/ and /y/ do not occur before [u] and [i] respectively, so sequences [wu] and [ji] do not occur.","ja":"半母音 /w/ と /y/ はそれぞれ [u] および [i] の前には生起せず、したがって連続 [wu] と [ji] は現れない。"},"type":"absence","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"none","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["w","y"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:shibatani1990@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0014-15","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-06-38-590Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:phon/glides-w-y--in-kuril-ainu-word-initial-y-hardly-ever","revision":1,"topic":"topic:phon/glides-w-y","topics":["topic:phon/glides-w-y","topic:phon/glides-w-y--onset-glides"],"statement":{"en":"In Kuril Ainu, word-initial /y/ hardly ever occurs, and when it does, other records almost always transcribe it with another vowel.","ja":"千島アイヌ語において、語頭に/y/が現れるものはほとんどなく、現れた場合でも他の母音で表されたものが同時に記されていることがほとんどである。"},"type":"frequency","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:kuril"],"quantifier":"usually","modality":"actual","conditions":["word-initially"]},"forms":["y"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:itabashi2001@pdftotext-pieces/l0005-07","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-06-38-590Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:phon/glides-w-y--although-ku-ipe-can-be-theoretically-assumed-as","revision":1,"topic":"topic:phon/glides-w-y","topics":["topic:phon/glides-w-y","topic:phon/glides-w-y--onset-glides"],"statement":{"en":"Although ku-ipe can be theoretically assumed as the base form, its actual pronunciation is ku-ype.","ja":"理論的には ku-ipe という形が基本形として仮定できるが、実際の発音では ku-ype となる。"},"type":"alternation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["ku-ipe","ku-ype"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0013-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-06-38-590Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:phon/glides-w-y--the-inventory-and-number-of-semivowels-are-identical","revision":1,"topic":"topic:phon/glides-w-y","topics":["topic:phon/glides-w-y","topic:phon/glides-w-y--overview"],"statement":{"en":"The inventory and number of semivowels are identical across all dialects.","ja":"半母音に関しては種類と数はどの方言も全く同じである。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["y","w"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:itabashi2001@pdftotext-pieces/l0001-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-06-38-590Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:phon/glides-w-y--the-glide-w-is-w-at-syllable-onset","revision":1,"topic":"topic:phon/glides-w-y","topics":["topic:phon/glides-w-y","topic:phon/glides-w-y--overview"],"statement":{"en":"The glide /w/ is [w] at syllable onset and weakens at syllable coda; careful [-uʔV] may alternate with rapid speech [-uwV].","ja":"/w/ は音節頭では [w]、音節末では弱くなり、丁寧に発音するときは [-uʔV]、早く発音するときは [-uwV] と言うことがある。"},"type":"alternation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"possible","conditions":["rapid speech"]},"forms":["/w/"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:murasaki2025@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0010-06","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-06-38-590Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:phon/glides-w-y--the-glide-y-is-j-at-syllable-onset","revision":1,"topic":"topic:phon/glides-w-y","topics":["topic:phon/glides-w-y","topic:phon/glides-w-y--overview"],"statement":{"en":"The glide /y/ is [j] at syllable onset and weakens at syllable coda; careful [-Vʔi] becomes [-Vy] in rapid speech.","ja":"/y/ は音節頭では [j]、音節末では弱くなり、丁寧な発音の [-Vʔi] は早く発音されると [-Vy] になる。"},"type":"alternation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":["rapid speech"]},"forms":["/y/"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:murasaki2025@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0010-07","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-06-38-590Z","status":"grouped"}
